        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7730bb72-c8a4-56fc-a120-77171eb3f95f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Helmut Rauca\n- Places: Kaunas Ghetto, Kaunas, Lithuania, Ninth Fort\n- Roles: Gestapo Jewish Affairs Specialist, Holocaust perpetrator\n- Events: Kaunas massacre of October 29, 1941, Große Aktion, World War II\n- Topics: Holocaust, mass murder of Lithuanian Jews\n\nFacts:\n- Helmut Rauca was born on 3 November 1908 and died on 29 October 1983.\n- During World War II, Helmut Rauca was a Holocaust perpetrator instrumental in the murder of more than 10,000 Jews from the Kaunas Ghetto in Lithuania.\n- On 29 October 1941, the Kaunas massacre, also known as the Great Action or Große Aktion, was the largest mass murder of Lithuanian Jews.\n- As the Gestapo Jewish Affairs Specialist, Helmut Rauca selected about one-third of the Kaunas Ghetto inmates, including men, women, and children, to be killed in the Kaunas massacre at the remote Ninth Fort on the outskirts of Kaunas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
